# Defense speaker notes

Mariem presents for 15 to 20 minutes. The notes are what she says. The slide is what she glances at if she loses the sentence.

- Easy spoken French. Short sentences. The scientific word that is already on the slide stays (F1-macro, ablation, NRC, SenticNet, attention). Do not swap it for a vaguer word, and do not add a harder one.
- Same order as the blocks on the slide, and the same words, so half a second on the slide restarts the sentence.
- Do not retell the slide in full. One sentence per block. Leave a number she can see, unless that number is the point.
- Dividers are one sentence. A result slide is a few sentences. Slides do not all get the same length.
- Notes she would say only if the jury asks stay on the questions slide, marked as such, and out of the timed talk.
